/; One module, brought by two spellings of the same path.
/;
/; The root compiled its brought files from a list deduplicated by exact
/; string, and "lib/counted-module.fg" and "sub/../lib/counted-module.fg"
/; differ as strings. The module was listed twice, so main called its init
/; function twice and its top-level code ran twice: "counted init" printed
/; two times. It must print once.
bring "lib/counted-module.fg"
bring "sub/user-module.fg"

println(counted::one() + user::two())
